摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"dsh-memory is a local, Git-backed long-term-memory plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH).","id":"gh:1339286962","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-memory","slug":"seriousz158/dsh-memory","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-bundle","dsh-plugin","memory"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"dsh-memory is a local, Git-backed long-term-memory plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH)."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-memory"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"`dsh-memory` is a local, Git-backed long-term-memory plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH)."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"It adds one persistent setting, a safe settings-page workflow for clearing memories, and an optional"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" idle-session synchronizer. The host plugin injects memory guidance only when `memory.enabled` is tr"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ue; the UI plugin lets a user inspect the repository state, toggle the setting, and clear learned me"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"mory through a deliberate two-step confirmation."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- Stores durable memory in a local Git repository, not in this source repository or a hosted service"},{"id":"p6s2","text":".\n- Registers the `memory` settings namespace immediately, so `memory.enabled` takes effect for the "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"next model call without restarting DSH.\n- Shows a long-term-memory row in DSH settings with reposito"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"ry status and a double-confirmation **Delete memory** action.\n- Preserves a Git recovery point befor"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"e clearing `summary.md`, `handbook/`, `rollouts/`, and `archive/`: a clean repository reuses its exi"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"sting HEAD, while dirty target paths get a dedicated checkpoint commit; the next commit records the "},{"id":"p6s7","text":"cleared state.\n- Refuses unsafe repository layouts, symbolic-link escapes, non-repository roots, and"},{"id":"p6s8","text":" path races during a clear operation.\n- Can process only idle local session logs through an optional"},{"id":"p6s9","text":" headless synchronizer. The synchronizer defaults to `workspace-write`, never silently installs DSH,"},{"id":"p6s10","text":" and forwards only an allowlisted environment."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Capabilities"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"This README describes stable user-facing behavior. Release-by-release\nimplementation details are int"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"entionally kept out of this page; see\nCHANGELOG.md and the GitHub releases\nfor historical changes."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### Local Git-backed memory"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- Memory stays in a local Git repository. There is no hosted memory service or\ncloud vector database"},{"id":"p10s2","text":".\n- Markdown records support front matter, namespaced ids, provenance, expiry\nprojection, determinis"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"tic conflict handling, and legacy compatibility.\n- `summary.md` is a short navigation snapshot; deta"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"iled knowledge belongs in\n`handbook/`, `rollouts/`, and `archive/`."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### Safe synchronization and recovery"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- Optional idle-session sync runs in a private per-run workspace. The model can\nedit only the isolat"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"ed copy; the host validates and writes the live Git\nrepository.\n- The host provides dry-run/preview/"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"apply flows, operation locking, health\nchecks, bounded batches, retry backoff, duplicate-id diagnost"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"ics, and\nmetadata-only journals.\n- Recovery/apply commits, rollback, backup export/import, and legac"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"y migration\nkeep changes auditable and reversible. Migration is available through the\nCLI/host API, "},{"id":"p12s6","text":"not the settings UI."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### Read path"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- When enabled, a bounded and explicitly untrusted `summary.md` snapshot is\navailable to the model ("},{"id":"p14s2","text":"12 KiB maximum).\n- `memory.search()` and `memory.context()` provide local, bounded retrieval\nwith so"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"urce citations and usage-aware deterministic ordering. Retrieval is\nhybrid: a derived SQLite index ("},{"id":"p14s4","text":"FTS5 trigram + CJK-bigram/word terms, stored\nat `.sync/search-index.sqlite` with restrictive permiss"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"ions) is fused with\nlexical scoring and exact-substring precedence, and transparently falls back\nto "},{"id":"p14s6","text":"a pure scan when the index is missing, stale, or corrupt.\n- Read usage is stored as private metadata"},{"id":"p14s7","text":" in `.sync/usage.json`; transcripts,\nprompts, credentials, and memory content are not written to jou"},{"id":"p14s8","text":"sync/usage.json`; transcripts,\nprompts, credentials, and memory content are not written to journals."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### DSH settings integration"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"The settings UI provides the memory toggle, repository status, recent-sync\nstate, preview actions, r"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ollback, and deliberate clear confirmation. It does\nnot expose the filesystem root or execute Git di"},{"id":"p16s3","text":", and deliberate clear confirmation. It does\nnot expose the filesystem root or execute Git directly."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"`v0.10.0` targets the DSH desktop app 0.2.x and keeps the 0.1.x web runtime\npeer range:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Component | Supported version |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| DSH desktop app | `0.2.0-rc.2` (peer range `>=0.2.0-rc.2 <0.3.0`) |\n| DSH web runtime peer range |"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" `^0.1.0-rc.6 \\|\\| 0.1.5-rc.1 \\|\\| 0.1.7-rc.1` |\n| Clean-room development test graph | DSH client pa"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"ckages `0.1.0-rc.7` |\n| Node.js | 22.x |\n| Python | 3.11.x |\n| Git | a local executable available on"},{"id":"p20s4","text":" `PATH` |\n| Operating system | macOS is the supported/tested integration target |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The package uses DSH's Cordis loader interfaces. The `rc.7` graph is the\nreproducible development an"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"d integration baseline because the registry's `rc.6`\ntransitive peer graph cannot be installed by pl"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"ain `npm ci`; this does not\nchange the host/UI packages' declared `rc.6` runtime peer range. DSH `rc"},{"id":"p21s4","text":".8` and\nlater releases are unverified until they pass this repository's test suite."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### DSH plugin bundle (recommended)"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"The repository root is also a public DSH bundle named `dsh-git-memory`. It\ncontains the host plugin,"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" the settings-page client bundle, and its\n`dsh.bundle` patch, so one install activates both halves:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"See docs/installation.md for the\ndesktop profile rules (aggregate bundle only, default memory root)."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"This project is distributed through GitHub source installs and GitHub Releases.\nIt is not published "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"oject is distributed through GitHub source installs and GitHub Releases.\nIt is not published to npm."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Restart the selected DSH profile after installing. The bundle does not include\nany memory data, sess"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"ion logs, credentials, or the local `.dsh` directory."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### Source checkout (development / local integration)"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Clone the repository and install its reproducible development/runtime dependencies:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The two workspace implementation packages remain private; only the root\n`dsh-git-memory` bundle is p"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"ublishable. This keeps the internal host/UI package\nnames stable while avoiding the already-occupied"},{"id":"p32s3","text":" unscoped `dsh-memory` npm\nname."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"Install the two local packages into your DSH profile. The installer defaults to\n`~/.dsh`. If you use"},{"id":"p33s2","text":" a non-default DSH or memory path, keep the same values in\nthe environment that installs, starts, va"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"lidates, and synchronizes DSH:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## Privacy promise"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"This repository contains code, tests, templates, and examples only. It must never contain any real D"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"SH memory, session log, credential file, browser profile, or user-specific DSH configuration. If you"},{"id":"p37s3","text":" believe sensitive data was committed, treat it as exposed, rotate affected credentials, and follow "},{"id":"p37s4","text":"sitive data was committed, treat it as exposed, rotate affected credentials, and follow SECURITY.md."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
